#: system.md:3
msgid "L99A T4 Lysozyme (T4L)"
msgstr "L99A T4 Lysozyme（T4L）"

#: system.md:5
msgid ""
"T4L has a specific mutation: leucine (L) substitution at position 99 with "
"alanine (A). This change creates a hydrophobic cavity in the C-terminal "
"domain, altering its stability and binding properties (see Figure)."
msgstr ""
"T4L では、99番目の Leucine（L）を Alanine（A）に置換している。この変化により C-terminal Domain に "
"Hydrophobic Cavity ができ、安定性と結合の性質が変わる（図参照）。"

#: system.md:7
msgid ""
"This variant is particularly useful as a model system for studying protein-"
"ligand interactions because the introduced cavity can accommodate small "
"hydrophobic molecules (benzene and its derivatives)."
msgstr ""
"この Cavity は Benzene やその誘導体のような小さな Hydrophobic Molecules を収容できるため、Protein-"
"Ligand Interactions のモデル系として特に有用である。"

#: system.md:11
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will use a structure based on the PDB ID "
"[4w52](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/4W52) with the CHARMM36 force field "
"and run a T4L-benzene dissociation simulation in the NVT ensemble at 300 K "
"using the velocity rescaling thermostat (see the `data` directory "
"[here](https://github.com/jakryd/plumed2-maze-tutorial) for more details)."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは PDB ID [4w52](https://www.rcsb.org/structure/4W52) に基づく構造と "
"CHARMM36 Force Field を使い、Velocity Rescaling Thermostat を用いた300 K の NVT "
"Ensemble で T4L-Benzene Dissociation "
"を実行する。詳細は[こちら](https://github.com/jakryd/plumed2-maze-tutorial)の `data` "
"ディレクトリにある。"

